steps.explanation:
$P$ lies to the right of both charges, so a positive charge pushes the field in $+x$ there and a negative one pulls it to $-x$:
$E_{1x} = kQ_1/(d+s)^2$ = 8.99×10⁹ × ({{Q1|C}}) / {{d+s}}² = {{E1|V/m}}
$E_{2x} = kQ_2/s^2$ = 8.99×10⁹ × ({{Q2|C}}) / {{s}}² = {{E2|V/m}}
$E_x$ = {{E1+E2|V/m}}.
